## Context

Upstream published v1.16.0 at `910310b` on 2026-09-07 21:49Z, and `main` now
sits one README-only commit further at `4467663`. The range from the reviewed
tip `5a81cee` is 14 commits and 54 files.

This is not a documentation release. In one evening the maintainer closed six
issues filed from here and merged one PR from here:

| upstream | subject | landed |
|---|---|---|
| PR #60 | vitest global temp-directory teardown (our ticket 0714) | `ed12d83` |
| #66 | a security policy; private vulnerability reporting | 21:19Z |
| #65 | annotation passages exhausted the semantic candidate pool before item dedup | 21:42Z |
| #61 | resolve the effective library once, route writes and annotation reads by it | 21:45Z |
| #63 | a transient census failure advanced the cursor and blocked catch-up on retry | 21:45Z |
| #64 | item-key bibliographies and CSL-JSON exports through the library router | 21:45Z |
| #62 | the `.mcpb` bundle advertised darwin/win32 and shipped only Linux binaries | 04:04Z 09-08 |

The source consequences reach the watched surface: `index-manager.ts` is
+338/-55, `src/router/library-router.ts` and `src/api/local-client.ts` are new,
`scripts/mcpb-bundle.ts` and a release gate are new, and `821629a` withholds the
index version stamp when an update cannot catch up notes and annotations. A
release-note-only update would leave the review baseline false, which is the
premise ticket 0735 established for the previous bump.

Ticket 0714's record stops at "staged, not sent". PR #60 has since been filed
and merged, so its third verification line — which reads as unmet *because* the
fix had not landed upstream — is now stale in the archive.

## Work

- pin `UPSTREAM` to `main` at `4467663`, naming v1.16.0 and the schema
  generation, and confirm that generation independently rather than carrying
  2 forward on assumption;
- read every changed watched source file; reconsider a requirement row only
  where a changed mechanism can move its verdict or invalidate its evidence,
  per the delta-bounded rule ratified at the 0618 bump;
- re-point every stale `SPEC.md` source citation the moved `index-manager.ts`
  and the new router left behind, and demonstrate the search for them could
  have found one;
- record the release in `SYNC.md` and `STATE.md`, and write
  `verification/UPSTREAM-1.16.0-REREAD.md` as the evidence report;
- append the upstream landing of PR #60 to closed ticket 0714's log, so the
  archive stops recording a fix as unsent that shipped;
- do not promote any row to `measured` on source reading, and do not carry a
  v1.15 measurement across a changed executable path.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `UPSTREAM` names `main` at `4467663`, v1.16.0, dated 2026-09-08, with the
      schema generation confirmed against upstream's own constant
- [ ] `verification/UPSTREAM-1.16.0-REREAD.md` accounts for the full 14-commit
      delta and every affected requirement row, and names what it could not check
- [ ] stale `SPEC.md` source citations are re-pointed, with a positive control
      recorded for the search that found them
- [ ] `SYNC.md` and `STATE.md` record the release, the six closes and PR #60
- [ ] closed ticket 0714 carries the landing of PR #60 in its log
- [ ] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check tickets/` pass

## Boundaries

No live-library mutation and no upstream post. This ticket moves the reviewed
source baseline; it does not close trackers 0613, 0648 or 0665, and it does not
manufacture an acceptance verdict for R15 or R22. The release-readiness review
running in parallel against `910310b` is a separate line of work and files its
own tickets; findings from it do not enter this one.
